TI  - Development and validation of two real-time PCR-methods for the rapid detection 
      of commercially available mussels and scallops in food.
PG  - 117300
LID - S0963-9969(25)01638-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.foodres.2025.117300 [doi]
AB  - Food allergies against bivalves are one of the most common chronic health 
      conditions in the world. With no existing cure, allergy sufferers must rely on 
      proper labeling of food contaminants. In this study, we developed two bivalve 
      real-time PCR systems for the detection of the commercially relevant species of 
      the two orders Mytilida and Pectinida. We have tested 23 species of bivalve 
      molluscs belonging to the above orders and have cross-tested our systems with 
      over 80 different animals and plants in order to demonstrate the specificity of 
      our systems. The Limit of detection (LOD(12)) is 1 pg for the Mytilida system and 
      0.1 pg for the Pectinida system. In food matrices a sensitivity of 10 mg/kg of 
      species per food matrix has been achieved for both systems. In addition, 
      practical application of the protocol was ensured by testing cooked and 
      autoclaved food samples. Finally, the robustness of the system has been confirmed 
      by testing multiple PCR parameters.
